						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														We love you Naysa. I wanted to do some research on J Boots, (Journeyman Boots), (also known as SoW   Boots), before responding. I would LOVE a pair of these and my eyes lit up when reading about your request for a raid for getting these. Unfortunately, you/we can not just kill a particular mob and receive them. It is a quest that must be executed perfectly to get them. The following is how to do the J Boots quest;<br />
1) At about 4pm (game time) start killing all the undead in south ro.<br />
2) At 6pm or 8pm kill the placeholder undead in the little tower.<br />
3) At about 12 Ancient cyclops will spawn... kill it to get no drop ancient cyclops ring, which is a bracer and adds 5 to int /shrug.<br />
4) Go to west commons and all the way in the corner of the zone kill shadow men until you get a shadow rapier.<br />
its a no rent item so you will have to finish before you log off.<br />
5) get 3250 gold (cant be 325pp)<br />
6) port to Freeport.<br />
7) zone to Rath Mountains.<br />
8) track down Hasten Bootstrapper and hail him.<br />
9) give 3250 gold, ancient cyclops ring, (it's actually a bracer), and a shadow rapier to him... and you have journeyman boots.<br />
<br />
Stats are:<br />
5ac, magic item, lore item, no drop.<br />
Effect: Journeyman Boots (which is like spirit of wolf).  Right clickable, no cast time.<br />
<br />
As a side note... this quest can be &quot;Piggy Backed&quot; or Muti-quested however you want to term it. If one person has the ring and the person who is getting the boots gives Hasten Bootstrapper the 3250 GOLD pieces, and the Shadow Rapier (found ours in WC) make sure whoever is getting the boots turns over those items LAST! You HAVE to be grouped for this quest too. You can lose out if you are not grouped.<br />
<br />
Here is the problem/situation that I see;<br />
According to other everquestians, (is that a word, lol), they are PHs for each other. Brother Zephyl is level 61 and 2 groups of 6, (12 total), are usually needed to take him down. Tough and FAST. The drake is fast and so is Hasten. <br />
<br />
If we get enough people and an enormous amount of time, (so all in group can receive J Boots), count me in.<br />
<br />
---Maktar (Nobel Alliance)						</td>
